{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984193-help-with-obsessions","id":984193,"title":"Help with Obsessions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-08T20:14:35-07:00","id":984193,"title":"Help with Obsessions","content":"Alright. So, I'm trying to get a feel for how to apply Obsessions and use them as hooks. I'm running a mage game where most of the players are in the process of transitioning between 1e and 2e. A lot of my players take obsessions related to their game traits, rather than any particular Mystery. &quot;Raise Gnosis&quot; is a simple one, but one which I have trouble determining how you might get 'closer' to or make headway on. &quot;Become a Master of Death.&quot; &quot;Become a Master of Life.&quot; Etc. Bearing in mind that these are starting characters, most of whom are a far cry away from Masteries, how might be some good ways for me to utilize Obsessions like this, to better draw in people into a particular storyline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:41:25-07:00","id":984207,"title":"","content":"For Obsessions of the form &quot;become a Master of X&quot;, seeking out and studying spells of Practices in that Arcanum above their own seems relevant, as does studying examples of the Arcanum's purview. Studying Ghosts might yield Arcane Beats for someone obsessed with mastering Death, for example - how do ghosts form? How do types of ghosts differ, and what causes one kind of ghost to form and not another? How can ghosts be banished or sent away, and what happens when you do? Study of souls could likewise yield insight into Death. And, of course, the study of death itself, especially given how broad a grey area there is between &quot;definitely alive&quot; and &quot;definitely dead.&quot; At what point does someone go from &quot;alive&quot; to &quot;dead&quot;? Does someone brain-dead read as dead? Etc.<br /> <br /> Studying biology, important life processes, and exotic living creatures could yield Arcane Beats for Life - what does birth look like under Life Sight? How does someone's Pattern change when they come down with a disease, vs while they're sick, vs as they recover? How do different diseases heal? How do various levels of injury affect someone's Pattern? Is natural healing fundamentally different from Life healing, or does Life healing just augment natural processes? How do the Patterns of &quot;higher&quot; and more complex forms of life differ from &quot;lower&quot; forms of life, and what do they have in common?<br /> <br /> (You may note that a lot of the examples I gave would be at the very least much easier to study by unethical means. This is deliberate; pursuit of Obsessions is supposed to be an ethical hazard.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:42:28-07:00","id":984209,"title":"","content":"I'd ask them to change their Obsessions. One, it's too broad which you've already noted, two it's not really a Mystery it's a goal so they can put that stuff in their Aspirations if they really feel like they need it. I'd encourage them to take Obsessions relating to the Chronicle, either tied into whatever Mystery the local Consilium has gathered around or on the Mystery that's at the center of whatever story they're currently in the middle of. They could come up with other possible Obsessions, like: Where do souls come from? Is Bigfoot real? etc. Basically, ask them to pose their Obsessions as questions they want answered, not as things they want to do. Let them know that any pursuit of an Obsession is going to lead to higher Gnosis or arcana anyway so if they make that their &quot;Obsession&quot; it's basically just a waste of story space for you and them. Obsessions that can be resolved relatively quickly are not a problem by the way, so you can keep that in mind too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-08-2016, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:54:18-07:00","id":984214,"title":"","content":"While I agree that &quot;become a Master of X&quot; is on the boring side for an Obsession (and I honestly have no idea what to do with &quot;raise Gnosis&quot;), I don't think it's fair to say that they're invalid as Obsessions. Obsessions are explicitly described as the arcane versions of Aspirations, and one of the example Obsessions given is &quot;become Wiser.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh, another possible activity for anyone pursuing an Obsession of that form - seek out a mage with greater knowledge of that Arcanum and get them to teach you (whether through cryptic discussions of philosophy, rigorous practice, being thrown into sink-or-swim danger, whatever.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:15:53-07:00","id":984227,"title":"","content":"How interesting a 'Become Master of X' Obsession is depends a lot on how far they are willing to go to learn and test their limits, as well as who they are willing to ask help from. Magic is learned through experiencing things, and depending on various factors you can make those experiences something to remember (and potentially highly traumatic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:17:39-07:00","id":984229,"title":"","content":"As stated these examples are pretty broad and while that might not seem to give the character much direction, it does give the ST a lot of leeway. A character whose obsession is to raise gnosis should be chasing after anything that smacks of supernal magic, mastery of Death means the character should be pursuing anything that relates to death, be it an outbreak of zombies, a haunted house or the discovery of a crypt full of perfectly preserved bodies from a century past. When your player says his character is obsessed with becoming a master of Death (Life, etc...), you should be hearing him say that his character is obsessed with death and will pursue anything relating to it Supernal or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:24:50-07:00","id":984231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984193-help-with-obsessions?p=984214#post984214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obsessions are explicitly described as the arcane versions of Aspirations, and one of the example Obsessions given is &quot;become Wiser.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Become Wiser&quot; is, however, literally the only way <i>to</i> raise that game trait, and it's steering a bit of your Gnosis back on itself to do so. Obsessions aren't <i>just</i> described as &quot;Aspirations, but with magic,&quot; either; these are things that give you an extra die on FMS rolls and serve as obstacles to convincing you to do stuff that would obviate them. Simply raising traits other than Wisdom isn't liable to be pertinent to many Mysteries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obsessions are just like long-term Aspirations, except they relate specifically to a mage\u2019s compulsion to <b>explore the mystical in her life.</b> They could be goals to learn or research specific things. They could be player goals for the character to encounter certain strangeness in the world. They could be goals to use magic in new or extreme ways. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T23:23:09-07:00","id":984275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984193-help-with-obsessions?p=984214#post984214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that &quot;become a Master of X&quot; is on the boring side for an Obsession (and I honestly have no idea what to do with &quot;raise Gnosis&quot;), I don't think it's fair to say that they're invalid as Obsessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was writing my post when you posted yours so I didn't see it. You have some good suggestions going on there, but I'd argue that each of your suggestions are separate possible Obsessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T00:34:06-07:00","id":984296,"title":"","content":"Look on the topics about Obsessions ( best are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974408-stories-of-obsession\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978264-training-wheels-order-path-aspirations\">this</a> in my POV ) and diversify them. Starting PCs have only one Obsession slot ( 2 if you use common house rule for giving cabal common Obsession ) so every one counts and using them on '<i>Becoming Master in X</i>' is just better used as '<i>Obsession: X</i>' - remember, the more broad Obsession, the wider net of possible Arcane Beat generating scenes you can use. And Arcana come out from various related phenomena, not only supernal magic of particular type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-09-2016, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:57:18-07:00","id":984789,"title":"","content":"This has been super helpful, thanks! I'll go ahead and see what I can work with this. I particularly like Mrmdubois' statements on to make the Obsessions a question. I probably won't make it a hard rule, but if the players have issues with coming up with them it sounds like a great way to set things up! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}